  (874, 152, 'What happens when zinc is added to copper(II) sulfate solution? Identify the products and type of reaction.', 'text', 1, 'Focus on the core principle of Displacement reactions.', '{"why":"more reactive metal replaces less reactive metal","sol":"Step 1: Identify reactants (Zn and CuSO₄)\nStep 2: Compare reactivity (Zn is more reactive than Cu)\nStep 3: Zn displaces Cu from solution\nStep 4: Write balanced equation","steps":["Step 1: Identify reactants (Zn and CuSO₄)","Step 2: Compare reactivity (Zn is more reactive than Cu)","Step 3: Zn displaces Cu from solution","Step 4: Write balanced equation"],"options":[],"conceptId":"chemistry_metals_displacement_reactions","skillId":"chemistry_metals","subskillId":"chemistry_metals_q1","subject":"chemistry","chapter":"metals","topic":"Displacement reactions"}', 0),
  (875, 152, 'In the reaction Zn + CuSO₄ → ZnSO₄ + Cu, identify the oxidising agent and reducing agent.', 'text', 1, 'Focus on the core principle of Displacement reactions.', '{"why":"oxidation = loss, reduction = gain of electrons","sol":"Step 1: Identify electron loss and gain\nStep 2: Zn loses electrons → oxidation\nStep 3: Cu²⁺ gains electrons → reduction\nStep 4: assign agents","steps":["Step 1: Identify electron loss and gain","Step 2: Zn loses electrons → oxidation","Step 3: Cu²⁺ gains electrons → reduction","Step 4: assign agents"],"options":[],"conceptId":"chemistry_metals_displacement_reactions","skillId":"chemistry_metals","subskillId":"chemistry_metals_q2","subject":"chemistry","chapter":"metals","topic":"Displacement reactions"}', 1),
  (876, 152, 'What is observed when zinc is placed in copper(II) sulfate solution? Explain chemically.', 'text', 1, 'Focus on the core principle of Displacement reactions.', '{"why":"Cu²⁺ ions are replaced and reduced to copper metal","sol":"Step 1: Zn reacts with Cu²⁺ ions\nStep 2: Cu²⁺ ions are reduced to Cu metal\nStep 3: Zn forms Zn²⁺ ions in solution\nStep 4: note visible changes","steps":["Step 1: Zn reacts with Cu²⁺ ions","Step 2: Cu²⁺ ions are reduced to Cu metal","Step 3: Zn forms Zn²⁺ ions in solution","Step 4: note visible changes"],"options":[],"conceptId":"chemistry_metals_displacement_reactions","skillId":"chemistry_metals","subskillId":"chemistry_metals_q3","subject":"chemistry","chapter":"metals","topic":"Displacement reactions"}', 2),
